Reproduce a lost-update on JSON documents then fix with field-level patching. Buggy Express handler, start verbatim:

app.put('/settings/:userId', async (req, res) => {
  const row = db.prepare('SELECT doc FROM settings WHERE user_id=?').get(req.params.userId);
  const doc = JSON.parse(row.doc);
  Object.assign(doc, req.body);
  await audit(doc); // async gap
  db.prepare('UPDATE settings SET doc=? WHERE user_id=?').run(JSON.stringify(doc), req.params.userId);
  res.json(doc);
});

Write a test where two concurrent PUTs updating DIFFERENT keys ({theme}) and ({lang}) race so one overwrites the other (audit awaits setImmediate), proving a key vanishes. Fix by applying patches atomically with SQLite's json_patch (or a synchronous read-merge-write with better-sqlite3 transaction) and keep the regression test asserting both keys survive 20 racing mixed updates. node --test green.

